127:Tbe6,*Waldems, July 2024 –* plastship is pleased to participate as a sponsor and exhibitor at the [4th International Recycling Forum](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/) organized by [RIGK](/partners/)in collaboration with the European Association of Plastics Recycling and Recovery Organisations ([EPRO](https://epro-plasticscircularity.org/)). The event will take place on **December 10 and 11, 2024, at the Dorint Hotel in Wiesbaden, Germany**, under the theme **"Networking towards a Circular Economy."**

The Recycling Forum offers a unique opportunity to actively shape the future of plastics recycling and discuss innovative solutions for a sustainable circular economy. Key topics include:

- Use of recyclates
- Design for recycling
- Innovative and chemical recycling technologies
- Collection and recycling of agricultural plastics

An accompanying exhibition allows for direct contact with leading companies in the industry. The last forum in 2019 recorded 150 participants from 22 countries. The conference language is English.

In addition to plastship, renowned companies such as [EREMA Group GmbH](https://erema-group.com/en), [Herbold Meckesheim GmbH](https://www.herbold.com/en/) and [Hessen Trade & Invest GmbH](https://www.htai.de/), with which RIGK has already successfully advanced funding projects in collaboration with plastship, are among the sponsors and exhibitors for 2024. Media partners [Circular Technology](https://circular-technology.com/en/), [Kunststoff Information](https://www.kiweb.de/), and [Plastics Information Europe](https://pieweb.plasteurope.com/) will support the high-caliber program and report on the speakers' contributions.

**Save the date and become part of the Recycling Forum**

The Recycling Forum is the perfect opportunity to further advance the circular economy with plastics. The entire value chain of plastics recycling is represented, both in the exhibitor area and among the participants. From raw material manufacturers to processors, recycling and technology companies, as well as EPR systems from around the world, the forum brings together all relevant stakeholders.

*“The forum provides a unique platform to discuss the latest developments and challenges in plastics recycling,"* explains plastship CEO Andreas Bastian. He adds, *"After our successful participation in the last forum, we are very much looking forward to sharing best practices with all participants. This is crucial to strengthening the circular economy and developing sustainable solutions. We look forward to shaping the future of plastic recycling together with our partners and forum participants.”*

Register for the forum [here](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/registration). We look forward to your participation and advancing the circular economy together.

If you have questions or suggestions, please contact me!

**Mirco Gattinger**, Marketing & Social Media Manager\
